bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    nogc_async_mut_missing_modules_2026-09-16, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep8: correction to the doc census - std.http_server.* resolves to src/lib/nogc_async_mut/http_server/ (~40 modules exist); only the three targets were absent (the two debug adapters already landed, re-verified). Implemented: async_handler_lifecycle.spl (bounded job registry: exactly-once completion, deadline expiry, cancel by job/connection/all, graceful drain, terminal reclaim, typed inbox completion); h2_async_dispatch.spl (multiplexed (connection,stream) registry, per-pair duplicate refusal, connection-scoped removal); tls13_record_adapter.spl (socket-neutral TLS 1.3 record adapter over os.tls13.record13: AES-128-GCM only with AES-256/ChaCha20 fail-closed per spec, split-record reassembly, 32 KiB cap). Also record13.spl fn to pub fn on the two suite fns (avoids 2 new visibility warnings) and one spec test syntax-ported to the supported Option narrowing idiom (every expect/fail unchanged - the as-cast of a Some-wrapped T? is deliberately fail-closed). Verification: 4/4, 1/1, 6/6; neighbours protocol_handler 8/8, worker_wire_shutdown 10/10, async_dynamic_dispatch 6/6, async_handler_registry 2/2, record13_checked_seal 21/21. Residual: debug/legacy_service_adapter_v1 3/2 pre-existing failures (debug lane). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/nogc_async_mut/http_server/async_handler_lifecycle_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/nogc_async_mut/http_server/tls13_record_adapter_spec.spl"

